          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "നീതി — nīti — \"justice\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ആ കുടുംബത്തിന് ഇനിയും നീതി കിട്ടിയില്ല. ā kuṭumbattinŭ iniyuṁ nīti kiṭṭiyilla. That family has still not got justice."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Justice is കിട്ടുക, received, or നിഷേധിക്കുക, denied."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "നീതി (nīti) is borrowed from Sanskrit nīti, \"leading, guidance; conduct\" (CDIAL 7546; Monier-Williams), from the root nī, \"to lead\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for giving reasons and opinions."
