              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "വിവേചനം — vivēcanaṁ — \"discrimination\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ജോലിയിൽ സ്ത്രീകളോട് വിവേചനം പാടില്ല. jōliyil strīkaḷōṭŭ vivēcanaṁ pāṭilla. There must be no discrimination against women at work."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Against a group: -ഓട് വിവേചനം (vivēcanaṁ)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "വിവേചനം (vivēcanaṁ) is borrowed from Sanskrit vivecana, \"discriminating, distinguishing\" (Monier-Williams). The Sanskrit word is neutral, telling things apart; Malayalam uses it for treating people unequally."
            }
          ]
        },
